## 7.5 Changing from sparkline to sparkbar

Instead of displaying the values as sparklines, we can display them as sparkbars as shiwn below.



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
reactable(
  report,
  defaultPageSize = 13,
  columns = list(
    Product = colDef(
      maxWidth = 200,
      style = list(backgroundColor = "#f3f1e9"),
      headerStyle = list(backgroundColor = "#f3f1e9")
      ),
    `Monthly Sales` = colDef(
      cell = react_sparkbar(
        report,
        highlight_bars = highlight_bars(
          min = "red", max = "blue"),
        bandline = "innerquartiles",
        statline = "mean"
        ),
      style = list(backgroundColor = "#f3f1e9"),
      headerStyle = list(backgroundColor = "#f3f1e9"),
    )
  )
)
```

